# Line endings are part of the contract here, not a preference.
#
# fixtures/ is regenerated by fixtures/generate_fixtures.py and CI asserts the
# result is byte-identical to what is committed. Without this, a contributor on
# Windows whose git has core.autocrlf=false commits CRLF, the Linux runner
# regenerates LF, and the reproducibility gate fails on every line of the file.
#
# text=auto eol=lf normalizes to LF in the repository and checks out LF
# everywhere, so the generator's LF output matches on any platform.

* text=auto eol=lf

*.png   binary
*.ico   binary
*.gz    binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
